Package: tulpaRatio
URL: https://github.com/gcol33/tulpaRatio, https://gillescolling.com/tulpaRatio/
BugReports: https://github.com/gcol33/tulpaRatio/issues
Title: Bayesian Hierarchical Models for Ratios, Rates, and Proportions
Version: 1.7.3
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", email = "gilles.colling051@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: Bayesian hierarchical models for ratios, rates and proportions,
    in which the numerator and the denominator are two processes with linked
    linear predictors and the ratio is derived from their joint posterior. The
    denominator is either a second response or a known exposure. Both
    predictors take shared or process-specific random effects, latent factors,
    intrinsic and proper conditional autoregressive fields (Besag, York and
    Mollie (1991) <doi:10.1007/BF00116466>), the scaled Besag-York-Mollie
    field of Riebler et al. (2016) <doi:10.1177/0962280216660421>,
    nearest-neighbour Gaussian processes (Datta et al. (2016)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.2015.1044091>), temporal random walks and
    autoregressions, Knorr-Held space-time interactions, and zero-inflated or
    hurdle numerators. The default sampler is the No-U-Turn sampler with
    hand-coded gradients; elliptical slice sampling, Polya-Gamma Gibbs
    sampling (Polson, Scott and Windle (2013)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.2013.829001>) and a nested Laplace approximation fit
    the subsets of models they apply to, and every fit reports the tier of
    guarantee its inference carries.
